From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:46:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: a hook for svc handlers in C and the start of
 libnx2linux_sync (#19)

An svc number can now have a handler written in C that runs before the
Python one and answers handled or not handled. The AOT code and the JIT code
go through the same aot_svc_dispatch, so a path cannot be missed. Horizon.bind
is the one place that says which logical thread a host thread acts for (a
guest thread, a fiber when it starts and at every switch). horizon_sync.py
loads libnx2linux_sync.so when NX2LINUX_SVC_NATIVE=1 (off by default) and
falls back to Python, saying why, when it is not built or does not fit.
The library answers no call yet, so nothing changes in a run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Prepare the kernel synchronisation calls in C: a native svc hook, Horizon.bind and the loader of libnx2linux_sync, off by default
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#19

